{"seq":14,"trial_id":"v02-pilot-2026-10/openclaw-haiku-mu-v02-dev/ms-01-quarrendon-tickets/r3","wall_ts":"2026-10-25T08:17:01.899Z","sim_ts":"2026-10-16T09:00:00-05:00","args_digest":"cd588c860483dc48a9b2dcb2472858f154fa2257eefe0ea2ae7d25c033df5045","actor":"assistant","via":"slack","tool":"chat.postMessage","kind":"write","args":{"channel":"C16V9M1OB60","text":"Ilse, I found three ticket numbers on Quarrendon Freight Lines. None were in #north-team itself.\n\n1. **QF-77031**, postmortem ticket for the 4 Nov 2025 Superior dock-schedule outage. It was posted by Dana Okafor in #inc-qfl-sev1 on 14 Oct 2026. It holds the webhook listener root cause.\n2. **#PD-4492**, Thea Ramaswell's ticket about Pemberline Dock gatehouse kiosk alerts at the Eau Claire yard. It is in Moss's \"Sunday prep for Ruth\" digest from 5 Oct 2025 (`teams/team-north/digests/2025-10-05-north-sunday.md`).\n3. **#4419**, Thea's ticket about gatehouse barcode scanners failing to read trailer tags at Door 14. It is in Moss's undated \"North cheat sheet\" (`teams/team-north/digests/north-account-cheatsheet.md`). The cheat sheet says it was escalated to tier-2 support for scanner firmware testing.\n\nTwo caveats for the QBR. The cheat sheet is undated, so I can't confirm when #4419 was logged. Also, the cheat sheet warns not to confuse Quarrendon Freight Lines with Quarendon Freightways, which is a competitor and not a customer. The Sev 1 room also spells it \"Quarendon\" in one message. I only counted tickets that clearly belong to Quarrendon Freight Lines."},"outcome":"ok","effect":{"channel":"C16V9M1OB60","ts":"1792159200.000126"}}
